adjudication.rationale:
In the new API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the webhook auth check is:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET)
  return 403;
```

If `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unset (thus `undefined`) and the request does not include that header (so `req.headers[...]` is also `undefined`), the inequality is false and the request is treated as authenticated. This is a real bypass condition present in the diff whenever `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` is true, because there is no explicit guard that the secret must be configured before accepting requests.
